{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale","id":43168,"title":"Trading Covers wholesale?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-05T15:32:03-08:00","id":43168,"title":"Trading Covers wholesale?","content":"Once Cover XP has been formed into a Cover, or a Cover has been claimed through a Soul Pact, can a Demon trade it away to another Demon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:12:46-08:00","id":43589,"title":"","content":"I believe that the thing demon's can trade/sell to each other is the contracts which give them cover. So a demon whose initial cover is a librarian who loves her partner could not trade &quot;is a librarian&quot; or &quot;loves her partner&quot; to another demon because that isn't expressed in a contract.<br /> <br /> In regards to cover xp used to form a cover. I think you could still trade those cover xp to another demon provided that those cover xp are a result of a contract. Also I imagine a cover may be reduced by one dot if you don't have the cover xp sitting around to represent the piece traded to another demon.<br /> <br /> That's how I would handle it if I was the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:39:30-08:00","id":43663,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd be inclined to allow it, but beyond the obvious costs to Cover I'd insist for a compromise. After all, go yanking organs out of a body, sometimes it's gonna go into shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:43:27-08:00","id":43667,"title":"","content":"This actually begs the question of why couldn't Demons enter into their own contracts with each other?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: the Descent, page 41</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So long as he has a functioning Cover, a demon is functionally a normal human with a human body and all that implies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, that section was referencing the physical flesh and blood of a Cover, but why couldn't Demons trade aspects of their Cover lives as another resource? (Mechanically, straight dots in cover)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:15:54-08:00","id":43721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale#post43168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once Cover XP has been formed into a Cover, or a Cover has been claimed through a Soul Pact, can a Demon trade it away to another Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly plan on allowing it. In fact, I think there are plenty of Unchained &quot;cobblers&quot; out there who receive broad strokes for what features and properties his client wants, then wheels and deals different pacts together to custom tailor it before trading it to the client wholesale (probably for a huge favor!). Since they also have perfect memory, the -really really- good ones probably have typed out conversations they've had, observations they've made, notes about what habits they've picked up, etc. and put all those notes in the folder with the pacts (or however they store it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-06-2014, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:15:42-08:00","id":43742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=43667#post43667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually begs the question of why couldn't Demons enter into their own contracts with each other?<br /> <br /> <br /> True, that section was referencing the physical flesh and blood of a Cover, but why couldn't Demons trade aspects of their Cover lives as another resource? (Mechanically, straight dots in cover)</div> </div> </div> </div>The quoted page deals with old age and infirmity and whether demons are physically human. The matter of pacts, I think, is not comprable to whether or not a cover ages.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the gaining cover section it discusses how one improves cover (115) and how one creates a new cover (116).<br /> <br /> In these sections there\u2019s no mention of demon-to-demon pacts for cover. An interesting thing to note is that on 118 in the last section where they discuss angel-jacking the writers indicate that only one demon can actually jack the angel\u2019s cover and how the entire thing requires demons to trust each other and have good will towards each other. This implies that the pieces of the freshly minted cover cannot be divvied up between all participants.<br /> <br /> The pacts section predominantly discusses pacts between a mortal and a demon but it has a section on p194 where they briefly discuss Pacts with other supernaturals. However this section does not mention demon-to-demon pacts at all. Given that the writers had plenty of time to consider whether demons could make pacts with other demons and did not mention it at all even in the section where they discuss how pacts interact with other supernaturals strongly suggests that demons cannot make pacts with each other.<br /> <br /> It is worth it to note that I don\u2019t think I came across a line which expressly forbids demon-to-demon pacts.<br /> The pacts section also does not deal with a pact between a mortal and two or more demons (i.e. either myself or my partner can collect on X) . Are these possible? \u2013shrug-<br /> <br /> In the end it\u2019s up to your ST and the story.<br /> <br /> I am not in favour demons making pacts with each other for pieces of identity. I think it would open up a new avenue where older more powerful and established demons can (and probably do) exploit the crap out of newer, fresher demons possibly stealing the literal shirt off the newbie's back.<br /> <br /> However, I also like the idea where if a team works together to accomplish a goal (angel-jacking) everyone should benefit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":"01-06-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:20:14-08:00","id":43853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=43721#post43721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly plan on allowing it. In fact, I think there are plenty of Unchained &quot;cobblers&quot; out there who receive broad strokes for what features and properties his client wants, then wheels and deals different pacts together to custom tailor it before trading it to the client wholesale (probably for a huge favor!). Since they also have perfect memory, the -really really- good ones probably have typed out conversations they've had, observations they've made, notes about what habits they've picked up, etc. and put all those notes in the folder with the pacts (or however they store it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like that idea. So much so I'm going to talk to my ST and see if he'd be cool with having a character like that in our game. That being said I don't think you can trade soul pacts that a demon has called in or covers if they're part of your demon. My interpretation of what I've read is that demons trade in open contracts, once a contract is settled it's part of the demon now so can't be traded. Though I guess a cardinal rule of rpgs comes into play here, mechanics should serve the story, if the story would be better like that, change it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:45:16-08:00","id":44159,"title":"","content":"My preferred interpretation at the moment is that you can trade aspects and pacts, maybe even cut off a piece of your cover and turn it into a trading card, but can't directly trade your entire cover. YMMV but the ability to perfectly take someone else's cover opens up more cans of worms for me than it opens interesting doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:11:08-08:00","id":44300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheFrigidMidget</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=43853#post43853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely like that idea. So much so I'm going to talk to my ST and see if he'd be cool with having a character like that in our game. That being said I don't think you can trade soul pacts that a demon has called in or covers if they're part of your demon. My interpretation of what I've read is that demons trade in open contracts, once a contract is settled it's part of the demon now so can't be traded. Though I guess a cardinal rule of rpgs comes into play here, mechanics should serve the story, if the story would be better like that, change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm currently playing around with an active/dormant cover system that allows Unchained to sever their connection to a given pact and either store it or trade it around wholesale. The main reason why I'm doing that is so it allows said &quot;cobblers&quot; the ability to make pacts and covers outside what their own Primum would allow, as well as giving any low Primum demon reason to keep making those deals and forging those identities - there's never a point where someone says &quot;well, I'd love to make a pact with them but I'm fresh out of Cover slots.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Side benefit 1: extremely paranoid Unchained can now have caches of dormant covers waiting for them if they ever have to go to ground. Side Benefit 2: when an Unchained dies, his peers are going to be <i>crawling</i> over the estate sale to see if they can get their hands on his pacts.)<br /> <br /> The mechanics I have currently are pretty simple: touching the pacts (or the demon you're trading with if it's a handshake deal*), spend a willpower point to X. Spend one to make an active cover dormant, freeing up the slot and allowing it to be traded, spend one to (re)connect with a dormant one, spend one to switch one active and one dormant pact, either demon participating spends one to trade one (or two!) active covers, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=44159#post44159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My preferred interpretation at the moment is that you can trade aspects and pacts, maybe even cut off a piece of your cover and turn it into a trading card, but can't directly trade your entire cover. YMMV but the ability to perfectly take someone else's cover opens up more cans of worms for me than it opens interesting doors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm the reverse, actually: I'm all for trading identities wholesale, but once a given pact has been integrated into an identity I feel like, barring the destruction of the pact itself, it's irrevocably part of the identity and can't be carved out. I favor this partly because I don't feel like tracking xp per pact once it's been spent, and partly because I like the idea that even though you can trade pieces and whole identities around with relative impunity, you best treat the actual integration of pieces into the whole with relative care and forethought since it can't be removed like a Lego Brick to be included in another cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> * At least one reason for handshake deals: rental covers.&quot;I'm lending you this cover temporarily but I'm keeping the paperwork hidden away so it defaults back to me.&quot; An agency favorite, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-07-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:58:49-08:00","id":44334,"title":"","content":"Mostly I worry about the implications for counterespionage. When anyone can sell out or get violently railroaded into selling off their cover, it raises tensions meeting up with a demon outside the ring (and inside most rings, really) even higher. I'm not sold on being able to 'shave off' aspects myself, it's just something I've been thinking over. The way I picture it, the demonic economy is dominated by trading pacts and information, with mortal and material assets as sidelines. Being a cover trader is less building it yourself and more playing quartermaster and forger, providing the right papers and ins to the client, but it's on them to bring the identity to life. The work of the cover trader also covers maintaining an inventory of pacts and making sure they're still ready and safe to go live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:05:41-08:00","id":44349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=44334#post44334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I worry about the implications for counterespionage. When anyone can sell out or get violently railroaded into selling off their cover, it raises tensions meeting up with a demon outside the ring (and inside most rings, really) even higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way I see it, if someone was in a position to sell or get blackmailed into giving away their identity, they're probably also in a position to sell out or betray the people they'd be meeting with anyways, even if it's not entirely voluntary. So relax! Tensions would already be that high in those situations. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:20:33-08:00","id":44359,"title":"","content":"That's true, the flavor of it just doesn't appeal to me. I like perfect disguises rarer. Good interlock material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T16:51:26-08:00","id":46590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/43168-trading-covers-wholesale?p=44300#post44300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm currently playing around with an active/dormant cover system that allows Unchained to sever their connection to a given pact and either store it or trade it around wholesale. The main reason why I'm doing that is so it allows said &quot;cobblers&quot; the ability to make pacts and covers outside what their own Primum would allow, as well as giving any low Primum demon reason to keep making those deals and forging those identities - there's never a point where someone says &quot;well, I'd love to make a pact with them but I'm fresh out of Cover slots.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Side benefit 1: extremely paranoid Unchained can now have caches of dormant covers waiting for them if they ever have to go to ground. Side Benefit 2: when an Unchained dies, his peers are going to be <i>crawling</i> over the estate sale to see if they can get their hands on his pacts.)<br /> <br /> The mechanics I have currently are pretty simple: touching the pacts (or the demon you're trading with if it's a handshake deal*), spend a willpower point to X. Spend one to make an active cover dormant, freeing up the slot and allowing it to be traded, spend one to (re)connect with a dormant one, spend one to switch one active and one dormant pact, either demon participating spends one to trade one (or two!) active covers, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that all sounds like exactly like what I'd like to see implemented in our game. It'll probably make my already paranoid demon that much more paranoid. Two thumbs up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}